# Blue Roster marketing

Follow `marketing/README.md` (local repo), then `marketing/foundations.md`, and `marketing/landing.md` or `marketing/banners.md`. Tokens: `tokens/marketing.css` (`--mkt-*`); details in `tokens/marketing.md`. Match the PNGs in `marketing/references/`. If the repo is not open: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/jpablomatz/blueroster-design-system/main/marketing/README.md

- Marketing layer only: do not use `--br-*` tokens or `br-*` components on marketing pages (product screenshots inside a piece keep their own look).
- Inter only. Black for display/H1 and banner headlines; H2–H4 Semi Bold.
- Light page; Navy `#002458` only as a band (`[data-mkt-band="navy"]`). No Dark pages.
- Buttons: `#064DB7` + White on light (Manufacturing too); White `#F9F9F9` + Navy text in Navy bands. `#1E75F6` is a non-text accent only.
- Orange `#F66C1E`: accent only. Navy text on it, never white, never a button.
- Text contrast ≥ 4.5:1. Banner minimum sizes (approved by István 2026-10-19): support/body ≥ 24 px, eyebrows and button text ≥ 20 px on 1080/1200 formats; Display ≥ 12 px. Story safe zone 250 px top and bottom. Layout (v6.2): copy-block spacing fixed (orange line, eyebrow, headline, support, button), no text overflow; logo top-left LinkedIn 64/56, Square 72/72, Story 72/250; button moves with copy (Story: logo, copy, button ~56 px, device); Square+phone: button bottom = phone outer bottom edge; Square+monitor: full content width ~48 px below copy, may crop at bottom; LinkedIn+monitor: copy top = monitor top; glow always with device; safe zone is for text/button/logo only, devices may enter it. Copy-block text layers use fixed width (block width or Fill), never Hug, so they wrap and never overflow their box.
- Approved stats only, per vertical. Never invent stats, quotes, testimonials, names or prices. Say "light version" (up to 50 users), never "free".
- Headlines verbatim from blueroster.com, sentence case + period. Links go in the first comment. Market: US only.
- Landing: all 3 next steps for everyone; Country = United States (default) · Other; consent lines exactly as in `marketing/landing.md`.
- Unknowns stay `TBD`. List Assumptions and Questions with the output.
